  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-24T21:13:39.360Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In lots of games when you want players to do something say learn about a feature you can set a quest for it, that way you know that a certain amount of players who have completed the quest have interacted with that feature.\n\nQuests don't fit VRChats theme really as the game is more of a chatting and meeting place than gameplay that quests would fit into but that's only a naming situation, for VRChat I suggest the name of goals.  Something to aim for a goal to accomplish.\n\nThis would help a big problem for new players of VRChat what do to?  Sure they can do the tutorial and there is advice on panels around home and hub but they need an incentive to do things so set goals they can accomplish.\n\nYet why should they do these goals?  Well you need something to reward them with achieving the goals and you have a new rank system.  The more goals a players finishes the more towards the next rank they get.  Or something like that.\n\nWhat kind of goals to set though?  Stuff like, Visit 10 worlds.  Favorite a world.  Change your avatar.  Favorite an avatar.  Make a friend.   All the way up to Upload an Avatar and Upload a world.  There are lots of goals that can be set.\n\nHope this is looked into.",
